  "description": "The emotion expressed is mocking contempt, conveyed through the absurd juxtaposition of the image with the text 'when did you have lunch?'. The meme implies that the subjects, likely Maasai pastoralists, are primitive or starving, which is a reductive and offensive stereotype. The humor is derived from this contemptuous framing, suggesting the subjects are incapable of managing basic needs like eating, thereby mocking their cultural practices and self-sufficiency.",
